Here is a patent text snippet drafted in standard legal and technical patent language:

***

An object of the present invention is to provide a highly precise, cost-effective, and scalable method for manufacturing an antenna substrate having integrated wiring and electrodes by utilizing a sequential photolithographic process, thereby enabling fine-pitch trace resolution and superior high-frequency electrical performance. 

To achieve the aforementioned object, the present invention provides a method of manufacturing an antenna substrate, comprising the steps of:

(a) preparing an insulating base substrate having a dielectric layer, and forming a thin conductive seed layer over at least one main surface of the insulating base substrate;

(b) applying a uniform photoresist layer over the surface of the conductive seed layer;

(c) aligning a photomask over the photoresist layer, the photomask comprising a predefined pattern corresponding to an antenna radiation element, an integrated wiring trace, and an electrode pad, and exposing the photoresist layer to actinic radiation through the photomask;

(d) developing the exposed photoresist layer to selectively remove portions thereof, thereby forming a patterned photoresist mask that exposes target region portions of the underlying conductive seed layer while leaving remaining portions covered;

(e) electrochemically depositing a principal metallic conductive layer onto the exposed target region portions of the conductive seed layer using the patterned photoresist mask as a boundary, thereby simultaneously building up the structural thickness of the antenna radiation element, the integrated wiring trace, and the electrode pad;

(f) stripping the remaining patterned photoresist mask to reveal the unexposed portions of the thin conductive seed layer; and

(g) differential-etching the revealed unexposed portions of the thin conductive seed layer to remove them completely, thereby electrically isolating the antenna radiation element, the integrated wiring trace, and the electrode pad on the insulating base substrate.
